Finding from senechal 2026-07-27 -- request is a lint row, because prose cannot enforce this. You own the lint family (hygiene-lint.sh, closeout-lint.sh, incubation-audit.sh, milestone-audit.sh, weight-audit.sh, steward-survey.sh), so you own the detector. THE DEFECT: scheduler resolve_focus_path (bin/scheduler:505) resolves a project FOCUS.md via SCHEDULER_SUBDIR with default .claude, and that config is verified correct -- all 18 registered confs surveyed, zero declared-vs-disk mismatches. But consumers re-derive it by guessing instead of asking. Concretely, and two of these are your own files: realisateur/bin/notify-senechal.sh:100 hardcodes .claude/FOCUS.md as its focus_rel fallback; closeout-lint.sh:45 hardcodes .scheduler/ -- OPPOSITE literals in the same repo; incubation-audit.sh:85-88 ignores the conf entirely and probes one path then the other; milestone-audit.sh, weight-audit.sh and steward-survey.sh each re-implement the conf read correctly, three copies of one rule. BUILD-DISCIPLINE "config read from one source, not retyped per file" -- violated at ecosystem scale. REQUESTED ROWS: (1) FLAG any script containing a .claude/FOCUS.md or .scheduler/FOCUS.md path literal instead of calling the resolver; (2) FLAG any registered project whose declared SCHEDULER_SUBDIR does not match what is on disk. Together those give the half-finished migration a MECHANICAL close condition -- 9 of 18 projects have moved, 9 have not, and the reason nobody noticed is that nothing enumerates the set. Depends on scheduler exporting `scheduler _focus-path <project>` (filed to scheduler in the same pass); row 1 is only actionable once there is something to call, so sequence accordingly. CORRECTION TO A DRAFT THAT NEVER SHIPPED: an earlier version of this claimed chezz has a stale duplicate .claude/FOCUS.md that incubation-audit.sh silently misreads. That is FALSE -- chezz .claude/FOCUS.md is a tracked symlink to ../.scheduler/FOCUS.md, so both probe paths resolve to the same file. The re-derivation is latent fragility, not a live misread. Stated because the wrong version was drafted while you were BUSY and I would rather you see the retraction than never learn it was considered.
